{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"extras","name":"Gripper, fingerprint sensor, MP3 player, 7-segment digit","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"A servo claw gripper that really grabs things, a fingerprint sensor (R307 / AS608, Adafruit_Fingerprint.h), the DFPlayer Mini MP3 player (DFRobotDFPlayerMini.h) and a single 7-segment LED digit.","category":"Modules","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// A servo gripper, a fingerprint sensor, the DFPlayer Mini and a 7-segment digit.\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ gripper\n// Its servo's pulse sets how far the jaws close: 1000 us (0 deg) wide open, 1500 us (90) shut.\nbench.device('gripper', (part) => {\n  const L = part.motor('jawL'), R = part.motor('jawR');\n  let v = 0, pulse = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      v = io.supply('V+', 'GND');\n      const p = io.pwm('SIG');\n      pulse = p && p.hz >= 30 && p.hz <= 400 ? (p.duty / p.hz) * 1e6 : 0;\n      if (v < 4 || !pulse) { L.limp(); R.limp(); io.draw(v >= 4 ? 0.005 : 0); return; }\n      const shut = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (pulse - 1000) / 500)); // 0 open .. 1 shut\n      const a = -40 + 45 * shut; // (jaw angle: -40 open, +5 pressing past shut)\n      L.to(a, v);\n      R.to(-a, v);\n      io.draw(L.stalled || R.stalled ? 0.6 : Math.abs(L.speed) > 5 ? 0.25 : 0.01);\n    },\n    status: () => [v < 4 ? 'no power (4.8-6 V on V+)' : !pulse ? 'no signal (limp)' : `${Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (pulse - 1000) / 500)) * 100)} % shut${L.stalled || R.stalled ? ', gripping something' : ''}`],\n  };\n});\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ fingerprint\n// The R307 / AS608 protocol: packets EF 01, address FF FF FF FF, type, length, data, checksum.\nbench.device('fingerprint', (part) => {\n  const keys = part.control('finger');\n  const NAMES = [\"Alice's\", \"Bob's\", \"Carol's\"];\n  let powered = false, finger = -1, fingerUntil = -1, now = 0, image = -1;\n  const buf = [-1, -1, -1]; // char buffers 1 and 2 (index 1, 2): whose finger they hold\n  const lib = new Map(); // id -> whose finger\n  let rx = [], out = [], log = '';\n  const reply = (code, data = []) => {\n    const len = data.length + 3;\n    const body = [0x07, len >> 8, len & 255, code, ...data];\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (const b of body) sum += b;\n    out.push([0xef, 0x01, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, ...body, (sum >> 8) & 255, sum & 255]);\n  };\n  const command = (ins, d) => {\n    switch (ins) {\n      case 0x13: reply(0x00); log = 'password checked'; break; // VfyPwd\n      case 0x01: // GenImg: a picture of the finger on it, if there is one\n        if (finger >= 0) { image = finger; reply(0x00); log = 'took a picture'; } else reply(0x02);\n        break;\n      case 0x02: // Img2Tz: the picture's features into buffer 1 or 2\n        if (image < 0) reply(0x15); else { buf[d[0] === 2 ? 2 : 1] = image; reply(0x00); }\n        break;\n      case 0x05: // RegModel: buffers 1 and 2 the same finger?\n        if (buf[1] >= 0 && buf[1] === buf[2]) reply(0x00); else reply(0x0a);\n        break;\n      case 0x06: { // Store: buffer -> an id\n        const id = (d[1] << 8) | d[2];\n        if (id >= 162) { reply(0x0b); break; }\n        lib.set(id, buf[d[0] === 2 ? 2 : 1]); reply(0x00); log = `stored ${NAMES[buf[1]] ?? 'a'} finger as #${id}`;\n        break;\n      }\n      case 0x1b: case 0x04: { // search the library for buffer's finger\n        const who = buf[d[0] === 2 ? 2 : 1];\n        const hit = [...lib.entries()].find(([, f]) => f === who && who >= 0);\n        if (hit) { const score = 80 + Math.round(Math.random() * 120); reply(0x00, [hit[0] >> 8, hit[0] & 255, score >> 8, score & 255]); log = `found #${hit[0]}`; }\n        else { reply(0x09); log = 'no match'; }\n        break;\n      }\n      case 0x1d: reply(0x00, [lib.size >> 8, lib.size & 255]); break; // TemplateNum\n      case 0x0d: lib.clear(); reply(0x00); log = 'library emptied'; break;\n      case 0x0c: { const id = (d[0] << 8) | d[1], n = Math.max(1, (d[2] << 8) | d[3]); for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) lib.delete(id + i); reply(0x00); break; }\n      case 0x0f: reply(0x00, [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 162, 0, 3, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0, 2, 0, 6]); break; // ReadSysPara: capacity 162\n      default: reply(0x00); // (LED control and the rest: fine)\n    }\n  };\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      now = io.time;\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3.0;\n      for (const k of keys.take()) { const i = NAMES.indexOf(k); if (i >= 0) { finger = i; fingerUntil = now + 2; } }\n      if (now > fingerUntil) finger = -1;\n      for (const p of out) io.send('TX', 'uart', p, 57600);\n      out = [];\n      io.drive('TX', powered ? io.supply('VCC', 'GND') : 0, 1);\n      io.draw(powered ? (finger >= 0 ? 0.065 : 0.03) : 0);\n    },\n    packets(list) {\n      if (!powered) return;\n      for (const p of list) {\n        if (p.pin !== 'RX' || p.proto !== 'uart') continue;\n        if (Math.abs(p.baud - 57600) > 600) { log = `heard ${p.baud} baud: it talks at 57600`; continue; }\n        rx.push(...p.data);\n        // whole packets: EF 01 + 4 address + type + 2 length + (length) bytes\n        while (rx.length) {\n          const s = rx.indexOf(0xef);\n          if (s < 0) { rx = []; break; }\n          if (s) rx = rx.slice(s);\n          if (rx.length < 9) break;\n          const len = (rx[7] << 8) | rx[8];\n          if (rx.length < 9 + len) break;\n          const pkt = rx.slice(0, 9 + len);\n          rx = rx.slice(9 + len);\n          if (pkt[1] !== 0x01 || pkt[6] !== 0x01) continue;\n          command(pkt[9], pkt.slice(10, 9 + len - 2));\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    status: () => [powered ? (finger >= 0 ? `${NAMES[finger]} finger on it` : 'no finger') : 'no power', `${lib.size} fingers stored${log ? `; ${log}` : ''}`],\n  };\n});\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ DFPlayer Mini\n// Frames: 7E FF 06 command feedback param-high param-low checksum-high checksum-low EF.\nbench.device('dfplayer', (part) => {\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  const led = part.screen('led');\n  let powered = false, since = 0, now = 0, ready = false, vol = 15, track = 0, playing = false, paused = false, started = 0, rx = [], out = [], loop = false, plays = 0;\n  const TRACKS = 9;\n  const frame = (cmd, param) => {\n    const b = [0xff, 0x06, cmd, 0x00, (param >> 8) & 255, param & 255];\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (const x of b) sum += x;\n    const chk = (-sum) & 0xffff;\n    return [0x7e, ...b, chk >> 8, chk & 255, 0xef];\n  };\n  /** each track a tune of its own: notes from its number (about 6 seconds) */\n  const note = (t, n) => {\n    const scale = [262, 294, 330, 349, 392, 440, 494, 523, 587, 659];\n    let x = (n * 7919 + Math.floor(t * 4) * 104729) % 9973;\n    return scale[x % scale.length] * (n % 2 ? 1 : 0.5);\n  };\n  const play = (n) => { track = Math.max(1, ((n - 1) % TRACKS) + 1); playing = true; paused = false; started = now; plays++; };\n  const command = (cmd, param) => {\n    if (cmd === 0x03 || cmd === 0x12 || cmd === 0x0f) play(cmd === 0x0f ? param & 255 : param);\n    else if (cmd === 0x01) play(track + 1);\n    else if (cmd === 0x02) play(track > 1 ? track - 1 : TRACKS);\n    else if (cmd === 0x06) vol = Math.max(0, Math.min(30, param));\n    else if (cmd === 0x04) vol = Math.min(30, vol + 1);\n    else if (cmd === 0x05) vol = Math.max(0, vol - 1);\n    else if (cmd === 0x0e) paused = true;\n    else if (cmd === 0x0d) { if (track) { playing = true; paused = false; } }\n    else if (cmd === 0x16) { playing = false; paused = false; }\n    else if (cmd === 0x08) { loop = true; play(param); }\n    else if (cmd === 0x0c) { ready = false; since = now - 0.5; playing = false; }\n    else if (cmd === 0x48) out.push(frame(0x48, TRACKS)); // number of files\n    else if (cmd === 0x43) out.push(frame(0x43, vol));\n    else if (cmd === 0x42) out.push(frame(0x42, playing && !paused ? 1 : 0));\n    else if (cmd === 0x4c) out.push(frame(0x4c, track));\n  };\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      now = io.time;\n      const was = powered;\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3.2;\n      if (powered && !was) { since = now; ready = false; }\n      if (!powered) { snd.stop(); led.set(0, 0, 0); io.release('BUSY'); return; }\n      if (!ready && now - since > 0.8) { ready = true; out.push(frame(0x3f, 0x02)); } // (its SD card found)\n      if (playing && !paused && now - started > 6) {\n        out.push(frame(0x3d, track)); // (that track finished)\n        if (loop) started = now; else playing = false;\n      }\n      for (const f of out) io.send('TX', 'uart', f, 9600);\n      out = [];\n      const sounding = playing && !paused && vol > 0;\n      if (sounding) snd.tone(note(now - started, track), (vol / 30) * 0.6, 'square');\n      else snd.stop();\n      led.set(0, 0, sounding ? 1 : 0);\n      io.drive('BUSY', sounding ? 0 : io.supply('VCC', 'GND'), 1);\n      io.drive('TX', io.supply('VCC', 'GND'), 0);\n      io.draw(0.02 + (sounding ? 0.1 * (vol / 30) : 0));\n    },\n    packets(list) {\n      if (!powered) return;\n      for (const p of list) {\n        if (p.pin !== 'RX' || p.proto !== 'uart') continue;\n        rx.push(...p.data);\n        while (rx.length) {\n          const s = rx.indexOf(0x7e);\n          if (s < 0) { rx = []; break; }\n          if (s) rx = rx.slice(s);\n          if (rx.length < 10) break;\n          const f = rx.slice(0, 10);\n          rx = rx.slice(10);\n          if (f[9] !== 0xef || !ready) continue;\n          command(f[3], (f[5] << 8) | f[6]);\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    status: () => [!powered ? 'no power' : !ready ? 'starting (reading its SD card)...' : playing ? `${paused ? 'paused' : 'playing'} ${String(track).padStart(4, '0')}.mp3, volume ${vol}` : `stopped, volume ${vol}`, `${plays} plays`],\n  };\n});\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 7-segment\nbench.device('seg7', (part) => {\n  const ids = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e', 'f', 'g', 'dp'];\n  const segs = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, part.screen(id)]));\n  const anode = part.params.kind === 'anode';\n  let lit = '';\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const com = io.v('COM');\n      lit = '';\n      let n = 0;\n      for (const id of ids) {\n        const v = io.v(id);\n        // a red LED lights from about 1.8 V across it, the right way round\n        const on = com !== null && v !== null && (anode ? com - v : v - com) > 1.7;\n        segs[id].set(0, 0, on ? 1 : 0);\n        if (on) { lit += id; n++; }\n      }\n      io.draw(n * 0.012);\n    },\n    status: () => [lit ? `lit: ${lit}` : 'dark'],\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"DFRobotDFPlayerMini.h":{"classes":["DFRobotDFPlayerMini"],"exports":["DFPlayerPlayFinished","DFPlayerError","DFPlayerCardInserted","DFPlayerCardRemoved","DFPlayerCardOnline","TimeOut","WrongStack","DFPLAYER_EQ_NORMAL","DFPLAYER_EQ_POP","DFPLAYER_EQ_ROCK","DFPLAYER_EQ_JAZZ","DFPLAYER_EQ_CLASSIC","DFPLAYER_EQ_BASS","DFPLAYER_DEVICE_SD"],"code":"// DFRobotDFPlayerMini.h, the parts most sketches use:\n//   SoftwareSerial mySerial(10, 11);  DFRobotDFPlayerMini myDFPlayer;\n//   mySerial.begin(9600);  if (!myDFPlayer.begin(mySerial)) { ... }\n//   myDFPlayer.volume(20);  myDFPlayer.play(1);  next(); previous(); pause(); start(); stop(); loop(n);\n//   if (myDFPlayer.available()) { myDFPlayer.readType(); myDFPlayer.read(); }\n// It sends the player's real 10-byte frames: 7E FF 06 cmd 00 hi lo chk chk EF.\nconst DFPlayerCardInserted = 2, DFPlayerCardRemoved = 3, DFPlayerCardOnline = 4, DFPlayerPlayFinished = 5, DFPlayerError = 6, TimeOut = 0, WrongStack = 1;\nconst DFPLAYER_EQ_NORMAL = 0, DFPLAYER_EQ_POP = 1, DFPLAYER_EQ_ROCK = 2, DFPLAYER_EQ_JAZZ = 3, DFPLAYER_EQ_CLASSIC = 4, DFPLAYER_EQ_BASS = 5, DFPLAYER_DEVICE_SD = 2;\nclass DFRobotDFPlayerMini {\n  constructor() { this.s = null; this.rx = []; this.type = -1; this.param = 0; }\n  _send(cmd, param = 0) {\n    if (!this.s) return;\n    const b = [0xff, 0x06, cmd, 0x00, (param >> 8) & 255, param & 255];\n    let sum = 0; for (const x of b) sum += x;\n    const chk = (-sum) & 0xffff;\n    for (const x of [0x7e, ...b, chk >> 8, chk & 255, 0xef]) this.s.write(x);\n    delay(20); // (it needs a moment between commands)\n  }\n  _poll() {\n    while (this.s && this.s.available()) this.rx.push(this.s.read());\n    const i = this.rx.indexOf(0x7e);\n    if (i < 0) { this.rx = []; return false; }\n    if (i) this.rx = this.rx.slice(i);\n    if (this.rx.length < 10) return false;\n    const f = this.rx.slice(0, 10);\n    this.rx = this.rx.slice(10);\n    const cmd = f[3], param = (f[5] << 8) | f[6];\n    this.type = cmd === 0x3d ? DFPlayerPlayFinished : cmd === 0x3f ? DFPlayerCardOnline : cmd === 0x40 ? DFPlayerError : cmd === 0x3a ? DFPlayerCardInserted : cmd === 0x3b ? DFPlayerCardRemoved : -1;\n    this.param = param;\n    this.last = { cmd, param };\n    return true;\n  }\n  begin(stream, isACK = true, doReset = true) {\n    this.s = isRef(stream) ? stream.value : stream;\n    if (doReset) this._send(0x0c);\n    // it answers when it has read its card (about a second): wait for that\n    const t = millis();\n    while (millis() - t < 2000) { if (this._poll() && this.last.cmd === 0x3f) return true; delay(10); }\n    return false;\n  }\n  available() { return this._poll(); }\n  readType() { return this.type; }\n  read() { return this.param; }\n  _ask(cmd) { this._send(cmd); const t = millis(); while (millis() - t < 300) { if (this._poll() && this.last.cmd === cmd) return this.param; delay(5); } return -1; }\n  play(n = 1) { this._send(0x03, n); }\n  playMp3Folder(n) { this._send(0x12, n); }\n  playFolder(folder, n) { this._send(0x0f, ((folder & 255) << 8) | (n & 255)); }\n  next() { this._send(0x01); } previous() { this._send(0x02); }\n  volume(v) { this._send(0x06, Math.max(0, Math.min(30, v | 0))); }\n  volumeUp() { this._send(0x04); } volumeDown() { this._send(0x05); }\n  pause() { this._send(0x0e); } start() { this._send(0x0d); } stop() { this._send(0x16); }\n  loop(n) { this._send(0x08, n); }\n  EQ() {} outputDevice() {} setTimeOut() {} reset() { this._send(0x0c); }\n  readVolume() { return this._ask(0x43); }\n  readState() { return this._ask(0x42); }\n  readCurrentFileNumber() { return this._ask(0x4c); }\n  readFileCounts() { return this._ask(0x48); }\n}\n"},"Adafruit_Fingerprint.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_Fingerprint"],"exports":["FINGERPRINT_OK","FINGERPRINT_PACKETRECIEVEERR","FINGERPRINT_NOFINGER","FINGERPRINT_IMAGEFAIL","FINGERPRINT_IMAGEMESS","FINGERPRINT_FEATUREFAIL","FINGERPRINT_NOMATCH","FINGERPRINT_NOTFOUND","FINGERPRINT_ENROLLMISMATCH","FINGERPRINT_BADLOCATION","FINGERPRINT_DBREADFAIL","FINGERPRINT_FLASHERR","FINGERPRINT_INVALIDIMAGE","FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT","FINGERPRINT_BADPACKET","FINGERPRINT_LED_BREATHING","FINGERPRINT_LED_FLASHING","FINGERPRINT_LED_ON","FINGERPRINT_LED_OFF","FINGERPRINT_LED_RED","FINGERPRINT_LED_BLUE","FINGERPRINT_LED_PURPLE"],"code":"// Adafruit_Fingerprint.h, the parts most sketches use:\n//   SoftwareSerial mySerial(2, 3);  Adafruit_Fingerprint finger = Adafruit_Fingerprint(&mySerial);\n//   finger.begin(57600);  if (finger.verifyPassword()) ...\n//   enrol: getImage() == FINGERPRINT_OK; image2Tz(1); (lift, place again) getImage(); image2Tz(2); createModel(); storeModel(id);\n//   find:  getImage(); image2Tz(); fingerFastSearch() == FINGERPRINT_OK -> finger.fingerID, finger.confidence\n//   getTemplateCount() -> finger.templateCount;  emptyDatabase();  deleteModel(id);  LEDcontrol(...)\n// It speaks the sensor's real packets (EF 01, address, type, length, data, checksum).\nconst FINGERPRINT_OK = 0x00, FINGERPRINT_PACKETRECIEVEERR = 0x01, FINGERPRINT_NOFINGER = 0x02, FINGERPRINT_IMAGEFAIL = 0x03, FINGERPRINT_IMAGEMESS = 0x06;\nconst FINGERPRINT_FEATUREFAIL = 0x07, FINGERPRINT_NOMATCH = 0x08, FINGERPRINT_NOTFOUND = 0x09, FINGERPRINT_ENROLLMISMATCH = 0x0a, FINGERPRINT_BADLOCATION = 0x0b;\nconst FINGERPRINT_DBREADFAIL = 0x0c, FINGERPRINT_FLASHERR = 0x18, FINGERPRINT_INVALIDIMAGE = 0x15, FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT = 0xff, FINGERPRINT_BADPACKET = 0xfe;\nconst FINGERPRINT_LED_BREATHING = 1, FINGERPRINT_LED_FLASHING = 2, FINGERPRINT_LED_ON = 3, FINGERPRINT_LED_OFF = 4, FINGERPRINT_LED_RED = 1, FINGERPRINT_LED_BLUE = 2, FINGERPRINT_LED_PURPLE = 3;\nclass Adafruit_Fingerprint {\n  constructor(serial) { this.s = isRef(serial) ? serial.value : serial; this.fingerID = 0; this.confidence = 0; this.templateCount = 0; this.capacity = 162; this.status_reg = 0; this.system_id = 0; this.security_level = 3; this.device_addr = 0xffffffff; this.packet_len = 128; this.baud_rate = 57600; }\n  begin(baud = 57600) { delay(100); this.s.begin(baud); }\n  _cmd(data) {\n    const len = data.length + 2;\n    const body = [0x01, len >> 8, len & 255, ...data];\n    let sum = 0; for (const b of body) sum += b;\n    while (this.s.available()) this.s.read(); // (anything stale)\n    for (const b of [0xef, 0x01, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, ...body, (sum >> 8) & 255, sum & 255]) this.s.write(b);\n    // its answer: EF 01, address, type 07, length, code, data, checksum\n    const got = [];\n    const t = millis();\n    while (millis() - t < 1000) {\n      while (this.s.available()) got.push(this.s.read());\n      const i = got.indexOf(0xef);\n      if (i >= 0 && got.length - i >= 9) {\n        const n = (got[i + 7] << 8) | got[i + 8];\n        if (got.length - i >= 9 + n) return got.slice(i + 9, i + 9 + n - 2);\n      }\n      delay(2);\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  _code(data) { const r = this._cmd(data); return r ? r[0] : FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT; }\n  verifyPassword() { return this._code([0x13, 0, 0, 0, 0]) === FINGERPRINT_OK; }\n  getImage() { return this._code([0x01]); }\n  image2Tz(slot = 1) { return this._code([0x02, slot]); }\n  createModel() { return this._code([0x05]); }\n  storeModel(id, slot = 1) { return this._code([0x06, slot, (id >> 8) & 255, id & 255]); }\n  loadModel(id) { return this._code([0x07, 1, (id >> 8) & 255, id & 255]); }\n  deleteModel(id) { return this._code([0x0c, (id >> 8) & 255, id & 255, 0, 1]); }\n  emptyDatabase() { return this._code([0x0d]); }\n  _search(ins, slot) {\n    const r = this._cmd([ins, slot, 0, 0, 0, 0xa3]);\n    if (!r) return FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT;\n    if (r[0] === FINGERPRINT_OK) { this.fingerID = (r[1] << 8) | r[2]; this.confidence = (r[3] << 8) | r[4]; }\n    return r[0];\n  }\n  fingerFastSearch() { return this._search(0x1b, 1); }\n  fingerSearch(slot = 1) { return this._search(0x04, slot); }\n  getTemplateCount() { const r = this._cmd([0x1d]); if (r && r[0] === 0) this.templateCount = (r[1] << 8) | r[2]; return r ? r[0] : FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT; }\n  getParameters() { const r = this._cmd([0x0f]); if (r && r[0] === 0) this.capacity = (r[5] << 8) | r[6]; return r ? r[0] : FINGERPRINT_TIMEOUT; }\n  LEDcontrol() { return this._code([0x35, 0, 0, 0, 0]); }\n  setPassword() { return FINGERPRINT_OK; }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"gripper","name":"Servo gripper (claw)","description":"Two jaws worked by a servo inside it (about 2.5 kg*cm): wire it like a servo (GND, V+ 4.8-6 V, SIG) and Servo.write(0) opens it wide, Servo.write(90) closes it. It really holds things: put a block between its jaws and close them, then lift the gripper while it runs. Glue it to a servo arm for a robot arm.","swatch":"#2a2c31","mass":30,"shape":[{"box":[3.4,2,2.4],"at":[0,1,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"box":[1.2,1,2.2],"at":[0,0.5,-2.2],"color":"#2a62c8"}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-0.3,1,-3.3],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red, 4.8-6 V)","at":[0,1,-3.3],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":7.2},{"id":"SIG","label":"SIG (orange)","at":[0.3,1,-3.3],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"jawL","mass":4,"shape":[{"box":[0.35,1.6,4.2],"at":[-0.9,1,3.2],"color":"#c7c9cc"},{"box":[0.6,1.6,0.4],"at":[-0.65,1,5.1],"color":"#3a3c42"}],"joint":{"type":"turn","at":[-0.9,1,1.2],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":2.5,"speed":100,"volts":6,"min":-40,"max":5}},{"id":"jawR","mass":4,"shape":[{"box":[0.35,1.6,4.2],"at":[0.9,1,3.2],"color":"#c7c9cc"},{"box":[0.6,1.6,0.4],"at":[0.65,1,5.1],"color":"#3a3c42"}],"joint":{"type":"turn","at":[0.9,1,1.2],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":2.5,"speed":100,"volts":6,"min":-5,"max":40}}],"device":"gripper"},{"id":"fingerprint","name":"Fingerprint sensor (R307 / AS608)","description":"Reads fingers and keeps up to 162 of them. Serial at 57600 baud (its TX to the board's RX, RX to TX), 3.3-6 V. With #include <Adafruit_Fingerprint.h>: Adafruit_Fingerprint finger(&mySerial); finger.begin(57600); finger.verifyPassword(); then getImage(), image2Tz(), createModel(), storeModel(id) to enrol, and fingerFastSearch() (finger.fingerID, finger.confidence) to find. Put a finger on it from the run panel (three people's fingers to try); it stays on for 2 seconds.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":20,"shape":[{"box":[2.8,1.8,4.2],"at":[0,0.9,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"box":[1.6,0.06,1.8],"at":[0,1.83,0.4],"color":"#6d8fb3"}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (red, 3.3-6 V)","at":[-0.6,0.3,-2.2],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":6.5},{"id":"TX","label":"TX (to the board's RX)","at":[-0.2,0.3,-2.2],"kind":"out"},{"id":"RX","label":"RX (from the board's TX)","at":[0.2,0.3,-2.2],"kind":"in"},{"id":"GND","label":"GND (black)","at":[0.6,0.3,-2.2],"kind":"gnd"}],"controls":[{"id":"finger","kind":"keys","label":"Put a finger on it","cols":3,"keys":["Alice's","Bob's","Carol's"]}],"device":"fingerprint"},{"id":"dfplayer","name":"MP3 player (DFPlayer Mini)","description":"Plays the tracks on its micro SD card through a small speaker (SPK_1 / SPK_2: up to 3 W). Serial at 9600 baud: its RX (through a 1k resistor on 5 V boards) to the board's TX, TX to RX. With #include <DFRobotDFPlayerMini.h>: myDFPlayer.begin(mySerial); myDFPlayer.volume(20); myDFPlayer.play(1); BUSY is LOW while it plays. (On the bench each track is a little tune: track 1, 2, 3... each its own.)","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":3,"sound":true,"shape":[{"box":[2.1,0.16,2.1],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[1.5,0.25,1.5],"at":[0,0.29,0.1],"color":"#b9bec7","collide":false},{"screen":{"id":"led","size":[0.25,0.25],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#30d158","off":"#0c2414","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[-0.75,0.17,-0.8]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","RX","TX","DAC_R","DAC_L","SPK_1","GND","SPK_2"],"at":[-0.9,0.16,-0.889],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","RX":"in","TX":"out","DAC_R":"out","DAC_L":"out","SPK_1":"out","GND":"gnd","SPK_2":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.2-5 V)","vmin":3.2,"vmax":5.5}}},{"ids":["BUSY","USB-","USB+","ADKEY2","ADKEY1","IO2","GND2","IO1"],"at":[0.9,0.16,-0.889],"dir":"z","kinds":{"BUSY":"out","GND2":"gnd"},"extra":{"BUSY":{"label":"BUSY (LOW while playing)"}}}],"shorts":[["GND","GND2"]],"device":"dfplayer"},{"id":"seg7","name":"7-segment digit (0.56\")","description":"One digit of eight LEDs (segments a-g and the dot dp). Common cathode: COM to GND, and each segment through its own resistor (220-330 ohm) to a pin: HIGH lights it. (Common anode: COM to 5 V, LOW lights a segment.) Pick which kind in its settings.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":2,"params":[{"key":"kind","label":"Its common pin","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"cathode","label":"common cathode (COM to GND)"},{"value":"anode","label":"common anode (COM to +)"}]}],"defaults":{"kind":"cathode"},"shape":[{"box":[1.25,0.8,1.9],"at":[0,0.4,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"screen":{"id":"a","size":[0.5,0.1],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0.03,0.81,-0.62]},{"screen":{"id":"b","size":[0.1,0.5],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0.33,0.81,-0.32]},{"screen":{"id":"c","size":[0.1,0.5],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0.3,0.81,0.32]},{"screen":{"id":"d","size":[0.5,0.1],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[-0.03,0.81,0.62]},{"screen":{"id":"e","size":[0.1,0.5],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[-0.33,0.81,0.32]},{"screen":{"id":"f","size":[0.1,0.5],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[-0.3,0.81,-0.32]},{"screen":{"id":"g","size":[0.5,0.1],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0,0.81,0]},{"screen":{"id":"dp","size":[0.12,0.12],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#2a1210","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0.48,0.81,0.66]}],"pins":[{"id":"e","at":[-0.508,0,0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"d","at":[-0.254,0,0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"COM","label":"COM (common)","at":[0,0,0.85],"kind":"io"},{"id":"c","at":[0.254,0,0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"dp","at":[0.508,0,0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"g","at":[-0.508,0,-0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"f","at":[-0.254,0,-0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"COM2","label":"COM (common)","at":[0,0,-0.85],"kind":"io"},{"id":"a","at":[0.254,0,-0.85],"kind":"in"},{"id":"b","at":[0.508,0,-0.85],"kind":"in"}],"shorts":[["COM","COM2"]],"device":"seg7"}],"examples":[]}